> idealeq x^2 - 1, x - 1 = x - 1
I = (x^2 - 1, x - 1), J = (x - 1) (grevlex, x, over Q): I = J
  reduced Groebner basis of I: x - 1
  reduced Groebner basis of J: x - 1
  check: each generator of the smaller ideal is a combination of the other's generators (cofactors multiplied out)
> idealeq x^2, y = x*y, y
I = (x^2, y), J = (x*y, y) (grevlex, x > y, over Q): J is strictly inside I
  reduced Groebner basis of I: x^2, y
  reduced Groebner basis of J: y
  check: each generator of the smaller ideal is a combination of the other's generators (cofactors multiplied out)
> idealeq x + y, x - y = x, y
I = (x + y, x - y), J = (x, y) (grevlex, x > y, over Q): I = J
  reduced Groebner basis of I: x, y
  reduced Groebner basis of J: x, y
  check: each generator of the smaller ideal is a combination of the other's generators (cofactors multiplied out)
